<title>CANADA: Canadian Gas Association storage survey - Feb 7.</title>
<headline>Canadian Gas Association storage survey - Feb 7.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Gas Association (CGA) weekly survey of Canadian natural gas in storage in billion cubic feet (bcf):</p>
<p>							 Pct Full  Pct Full</p>
<p>		 02/07/97  01/31/97  Pct Full  Week Ago  Year Ago</p>
<p>East	     72.91     83.31    31.35	35.83     19.8</p>
<p>West	     77.93     79.09    30.08	30.52     35.9</p>
<p>Total Canada  150.84    162.40    30.68	33.03     26.3</p>
<p>East-West division is the Manitoba/Saskatchewan and North Dakota/Minnesota borders.</p>
<p>East capacity 02/07/97: 232.55 bcf, 01/31/97: 232.55 bcf.  </p>
<p>West capacity 02/07/97: 259.11 bcf, 01/31/96: 259.11 bcf.</p>
<p>The Canadian Gas Association survey includes liquefied petroleum gas, all Canadian operators of gas storage and Canadian companies contracting gas storage in the U.S.</p>
<p>((--Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
</text>
